From e79474a2e087cd18533c31fc853806e9a0363ad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:47:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the devtools panel's notices speak pt-BR

The devtools panel's notices (0063) read their text through zeo_i18n's t!
from locales/<language>/devtools.ftl, in en-US and pt-BR: Chromium (or Edge)
not found, no local project, the open failure, no dev script (and the
untrusted dev_command case), the dev server that never announced itself, and
nothing to stop. The en-US file is the code's English byte for byte; the two
sentences that were glued from constants are whole messages now.

Not here: the wire errors the browser extension receives (browser_wire.rs),
which zeo-browser localizes itself, and the sidebar's devtools entries, which
sit in Zed's own sidebar.

In the devtools-panel group, after 0063.
---

